# WHAT THIS FILE DOES:
# Git normally tracks every file in this folder. This file tells Git
# to IGNORE certain files/folders entirely - they'll never be staged,
# committed, or pushed, even with "git add ." You don't need to do
# anything with this file day-to-day; it works automatically in the
# background. The categories below are junk that gets regenerated
# automatically on every machine (cached Python bytecode, virtual
# environments, editor config, OS clutter) - none of it belongs in
# the shared repo since it's either huge, machine-specific, or both.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
